            <ArticleTitle>Mouse Behavior Tracker: An economical method for tracking behavior in home cages.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>215-220</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2144/000114607</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Analysis of mouse behavior often requires expensive equipment and transfer of the mice to new test environments, which could trigger confounding behavior alterations. Here, we describe a system for tracking mouse behavior in home cages using a low-cost USB webcam and free software (Fiji and wrMTrck). We demonstrate the effectiveness of this method by tracking differences in distance traveled, speed, and movement tracks between wild-type mice and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) model mice (SOD1G93A).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
